title VerificationEvidence status (verification_evidence.status)
[*] --> PENDING : submitLecturerVerification() /\nrequestVerification() /\nstudent-affiliation submit
[*] --> VERIFIED : [institutional email domain\nmatch] (affiliation.service)
PENDING --> VERIFIED : decideVerification()\n[approve]
PENDING --> NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION : decideVerification()\n[more_info]
PENDING --> REJECTED : decideVerification() [reject]
PENDING --> INVALIDATED : [profile position, institution\nor identity changed]
NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION --> INVALIDATED : [position or affiliation\ntarget changed]
NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION --> NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION : user resubmits\n/ supersededAt set
VERIFIED --> VERIFIED : [position change]\n/ invalidatedAt set only
REJECTED --> [*]
INVALIDATED --> [*]
legend bottom
  Rows are created directly as PENDING (or VERIFIED by email
  domain match). Resubmission after NEEDS_MORE_INFORMATION
  creates a NEW row (revision+1, previousRequestId) in PENDING.

  <b>Dead values</b>: UNVERIFIED, NOT_SUBMITTED and EXPIRED are allowed by the DB CHECK constraint but
  no code writes them on this table. Retention cleanup removes
  files only; it does not set EXPIRED.
endlegend
@enduml
